        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/fa3940e8-da58-42db-828d-5ec1d7758959,1723651719370/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C999%2C561%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A woman coughing shields her mouth with her fist. ' width='620' height='349' title='Close Up Of Woman Suffering With Cough; Shutterstock ID 702337306'/><p>Research shows a growing number of non- and never-smokers are getting diagnosed with lung cancer. Risks for never-smokers include poor air quality caused by pollution and wildfire smoke, occupational exposures like those for firefighters and construction workers, as well as cancer-causing gases like radon found in an increasing number of homes.</p>",
